 "description": "A juvenile Belatz: 2 body regions (B2), a head, 2 eyes, a 2-leaf crest, 2 legs, 2 flaps, a tail; feathers; upright, neck head. Coat: colour lagoon; fluff long and swept; sheen between; feathers long; fur reach bushy tail; second colour butter. Face: head between; beak long; crest tall; crown tall; eyes between. Shape: waist thin; back line arched; hind body between; body pear; build high. Legs & tail: tail curl curls up; tail between. Proportions: a large body, a long beak, a tall crest, a tall feather crest, long legs, broad feet, a thin waist, an arched back, the tail curled up, wide flaps. Posture: standing upright on its two legs, weight on its broad feet, body held level, still, looking at the viewer.",
